Description: Set the docked DevTools origin for touch transferred to Viz
 The docked DevTools content view is not at the compositor surface origin.
 On Android 16+ with InputOnViz, touch sequences transferred to Viz arrive
 in compositor surface coordinates, so without the view's origin Viz offset
 DevTools touches by the view's position (the toolbar height, plus the side UI
 width). Pass it through EventForwarder#setContainerViewOriginInCompositorSurface
 (see the backport in 0006).
Author: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Forwarded: not-needed

--- a/chrome/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/compositor/DockedDevToolsHost.java
+++ b/chrome/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/compositor/DockedDevToolsHost.java
@@ -239,6 +239,11 @@ class DockedDevToolsHost implements DevT
             params.topMargin = top;
             contentView.setLayoutParams(params);
         }
+        // Touch sequences transferred to Viz arrive in compositor surface coordinates, which
+        // match this holder's. Let Viz account for where the DevTools content view is placed.
+        devToolsWebContents
+                .getEventForwarder()
+                .setContainerViewOriginInCompositorSurface(left, top);
         mHolder.getCompositorView()
                 .onPhysicalBackingSizeChanged(devToolsWebContents, width, height);
         devToolsWebContents.setSize(width, height);
